# Quarto rendered output — regenerated on every build, never committed by hand
/_site/
/.quarto/

# Stray STANDALONE renders. Rendering a single .qmd outside the project context
# (VS Code's Render button can do this) writes the page and its asset folder
# NEXT TO the source instead of into _site/. Two reasons these must never be
# committed: they are build output, and Quarto treats unrecognised files in the
# project folder as resources — so a leftover index.html here can be copied over
# the freshly built _site/index.html and put a stale page on the live site.
# There are no hand-written .html source files in this project; every page is a
# .qmd, so anything matching these names is output.
/index.html
/research.html
/teaching.html
/site_libs/

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/

# Safety net: never let anything from the private area in, even if misplaced here.
# (private/ lives OUTSIDE this folder by design; this is belt-and-braces.)
**/private/
tracking.*
*-source/

**/*.quarto_ipynb
